# Sambac Clair — Green Petal / Soft Woods — 30 mL V1

> SUPERSEDED 2026-09-08: the user confirmed Romandolide is out of stock. Use [the stock-corrected V2](Jasmine_Sambac_Clair_30mL_V2.md) for the current draft. V1's original recipe and diagnostic below are preserved as history, not current compounding authority.

Date: 2026-09-08.

**Status: FORMULATION DRAFT / NOT SKIN-RELEASED / CLEAN DRYDOWN NOT TESTED.**

The recipe is a current-inventory design candidate, not an indole-free perfume or a validated sensory result. The requested direction is unisex, recognizable jasmine with leafy freshness, restrained woods and a soft creamy base. Jasmine Sambac absolute remains mandatory. No separate indole, skatole, PCME, vanilla, peach lactone, smoke or leather is added.

## Batch and stock basis

- Final volume target: **30.00 mL**.
- Concentrate target: **6000 uL** of supplied stocks, nominally 6.00 mL.
- Ethanol 96%: **q.s. to 30.00 mL final volume**; about 24 mL, not an assertion that mixed liquid volumes add exactly.
- Nominal supplied-stock loading: **20% by recipe volume**. This is not 20% neat aromatic material and not 20% w/w.
- Jasmine Sambac: **10% w/w in DPG**, confirmed directly by the user on 2026-09-08. Do not use Jasmine FO, Blossoms base, neat Sambac, or a differently diluted stock in its place.
- Other rows below use the undiluted stock forms implied by the live inventory, where no numerical dilution is listed. Bottle labels still govern; any further dilution requires recalculation.
- No prepared stock has been physically checked for remaining amount, age or condition.

## Formula — physical basket order

Amounts descend within each basket; the upward reset at a new basket is intentional. All ingredient transfers are at least 60 uL for the 30 mL recipe. The ppm column is an **estimated w/w concentration in the complete supplied-stock concentrate**, using a clearly stated uniform density approximation of 1.000 g/mL. It is not an exact mass result; see the accounting section.

